# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Small Plates, Big Stakes — environment variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Copy this file to ".env.local"        ->  cp .env.example .env.local
# 2. Paste your Supabase project values below.
# 3. Restart the dev server.
#
# If these are left blank / missing, the app automatically runs in DEMO MODE
# with realistic mock vote data (and a simulated live feed) so the UI still works
# locally with zero setup. Perfect for previewing before wiring up Supabase.
#
# Find these in your Supabase dashboard:  Project Settings -> API
#   - Project URL   ->  VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   - anon public   ->  VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   (safe to expose in the browser)
#
# NOTE: Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the client.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-goes-here
